# hlsdemux creates an output stream for every rendition of the selected variant except
# SUBTITLES: setup_streams passes `selected` as VIDEO || AUDIO and create_stream_for_playlist
# returns without creating anything for a stream that is not selected, so a master playlist
# whose subtitles live in their own EXT-X-MEDIA rendition exposes no text stream at all.
#
# Selecting the rendition is only half of it. A WebVTT fragment carries its cue times on its
# own timeline and ties that timeline to the presentation with an X-TIMESTAMP-MAP header, so
# the cue times have to be converted before they mean anything to a player. The successor
# element does that in ext/adaptivedemux2/hls/gsthlsdemux-util.c against a map of internal
# (MPEG-TS) time to stream time; this carries that conversion over, taking the map from the
# primary stream's first PCR and the stream time of the fragment it came from -- both of
# which this element already computes. Where the successor's fallbacks apply they are kept
# verbatim: a fragment with no X-TIMESTAMP-MAP is read as carrying MPEG-TS values, a cue that
# cannot be converted because no primary fragment has provided a PCR yet keeps its original
# value, and a cue that converts to a negative stream time is clamped to zero.
#
# A subtitle rendition otherwise travels the path the audio renditions already take: its
# fragments are typefound (WebVTT types as application/x-subtitle-vtt) and pushed as their own
# stream, and is_primary_playlist stays false for every rendition, so bitrate switching keeps
# following the main playlist.
#
# Applied by build_deps with patch -p1.
